dopplerloc - third-party data, services and software
=====================================================
The dopplerloc program code is licensed under the licence in the LICENSE file. The items below are NOT covered by that
licence: each keeps its own terms. Credits are repeated in README.md and at the bottom of the web page.

BUNDLED DATA (dopplerloc/data/, see dopplerloc/data/DATA_LICENSES.md)
- Places (countries, states, cities): dr5hn/countries-states-cities-database, Open Database Licence (ODbL) 1.0,
  https://github.com/dr5hn/countries-states-cities-database ; and GeoNames, Creative Commons Attribution 4.0,
  https://www.geonames.org (read through the `geonamescache` package).
- Country bounding boxes: sandstrom/country-bounding-boxes, built from Natural Earth (public domain),
  https://github.com/sandstrom/country-bounding-boxes
- Time zones per country: IANA time zone database (zone.tab), public domain.
- Aircraft engine types (typecodes.csv): derived from Berkanktk/datasets `all_aircrafts.csv` (https://github.com/Berkanktk/datasets),
  which is based on ICAO Doc 8643 aircraft type designators. That repository is MIT-licensed for the project itself, and states that
  its aircraft data is "per source license" (ICAO Doc 8643). The file here keeps only three facts per type designator (code, engine
  type, class). ICAO Doc 8643 remains the original source; check ICAO's terms before redistributing or using it commercially.

DATA DOWNLOADED WHEN YOU RUN THE PROGRAM (not included in this package)
- Flight history: adsb.lol "globe_history" daily archives, Open Database Licence (ODbL) 1.0,
  https://www.adsb.lol/docs/open-data/historical/ . Contains data from adsb.lol feeders and friends. If you publish a database or
  results derived from it, give attribution and check the ODbL share-alike terms.
- Flight history (optional): OpenSky Network, https://opensky-network.org , via the `pyopensky` library. Use is subject to OpenSky's
  terms (access to historical data is restricted, mainly to research, government and aviation authorities). If you publish results
  that use OpenSky data, follow OpenSky's citation guidance on their website.
- Aircraft registry / type list: wiedehopf/tar1090-db, https://github.com/wiedehopf/tar1090-db (see its repository for licence terms).
- Elevation: Terrain Tiles on AWS (Terrarium format), https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/ . Attribution is required. The tiles are
  built from 3DEP, SRTM and GMTED2010 data courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey, ETOPO1 (NOAA), and national sources including
  Copernicus EU-DEM (produced using Copernicus data and information funded by the European Union), Geoscience Australia, Land
  Information New Zealand, INEGI (Mexico), Environment Agency (UK), Open Government Licence - Canada, Kartverket (Norway) and
  ArcticDEM. Full list: https://github.com/tilezen/joerd/blob/master/docs/attribution.md
- Map tiles: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright . Follow the OSM tile usage policy.

LIBRARIES AND SERVICES USED BY THE PAGE
- Leaflet (BSD-2-Clause), https://leafletjs.com
- Inter font (SIL Open Font Licence 1.1), loaded from Google Fonts
- Python packages: numpy, scipy, pandas, pyarrow, Flask, Pillow, tzdata, certifi, truststore, orjson (each under its own licence;
  see their packages); imageio-ffmpeg downloads an FFmpeg build (FFmpeg is LGPL/GPL, https://ffmpeg.org); exiftool (optional,
  https://exiftool.org); pyopensky (optional, see its repository for licence).

